title: Healthcare workers strike!
subtitle: Primary-care doctors demand staff expansion
new-page: true
tags: event
role: event
face-image: img/events/vaga_health.jpg
max-visits: 1
view-if: strike_triggered = "healthcare" and not cat_caretaker_gov and healthcare_spending >= -2 and healthcare_spending < 2
on-arrival: {!
    Q.strike_timer = 6;
    Q.strike_healthcare_response = null;
    Q.strike_healthcare_settled = false;
    Q.strike_healthcare_partner = Q.health_minister_party;
    if (["indp.", "ind.", "independent"].includes(Q.strike_healthcare_partner)) Q.strike_healthcare_partner = Q.president_party;
    if (Q.strike_healthcare_partner == "ciu") Q.strike_healthcare_partner = Q.parlament_current_ciu;
    if (Q.strike_healthcare_partner == "federal_left") Q.strike_healthcare_partner = Q.parlament_current_icv;
    Q.strike_healthcare_relations = Q[Q.strike_healthcare_partner + "_relations"];
    if (["jxsi", "jxcat"].includes(Q.strike_healthcare_partner) && !Number.isFinite(Q.strike_healthcare_relations))
        Q.strike_healthcare_relations = Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_relations"];
!}

= Healthcare workers strike!

Primary-care doctors demand more staff to be able to guarantee minimum consultation times of, at the very least, twelve minutes per patient. Doctors are taking to the streets, putting enormous pressure on [? if health_minister_gender = "m": Conseller ?][? if health_minister_gender = "f": Consellera ?]of Health [+ health_minister +]. What will our position be?

- @accept
- @pressure
- @protest
- @quiet

@accept
title: Accept the workers' demands
view-if: health_minister_party = player_party or (player_in_jxsi and health_minister_party = "jxsi") or (player_in_jxcat and health_minister_party = "jxcat")
subtitle: We control the ministry after all. \[-1 budget\]
choose-if: government_budget >= 1 and healthcare_spending >= 0 and social_spending_cap >= 0 and not fla_escalated
unavailable-subtitle: [? if government_budget < 1: Not enough budget. ?][? if healthcare_spending < 0: Healthcare cuts need to be reversed before such a measure would even be possible. ?][? if social_spending_cap < 0: The current social spending cap is too low to allow for this. ?][? if fla_escalated: Stringent FLA conditions ban us from taking such action. ?]
on-arrival: strike_healthcare_response = "accept"
go-to: resolve

@pressure
title: Push [+ health_minister_party +] to accept the workers' demands
view-if: not (health_minister_party = player_party or (player_in_jxsi and health_minister_party = "jxsi") or (player_in_jxcat and health_minister_party = "jxcat")) and ((player_party = "erc" and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting)) or (player_party = "cup" and (cup_in_gob or cup_supporting)) or (player_in_jxsi and (jxsi_in_gob or jxsi_supporting)) or (player_in_jxcat and (jxcat_in_gob or jxcat_supporting)))
subtitle: We'll have to apply pressure on [+ health_minister_party +] for them to even consider sitting down with the union representatives. \[-1 resources; -1 budget\]
choose-if: (not (health_minister_party = player_party or (player_in_jxsi and health_minister_party = "jxsi") or (player_in_jxcat and health_minister_party = "jxcat")) and ((player_party = "erc" and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting)) or (player_party = "cup" and (cup_in_gob or cup_supporting)) or (player_in_jxsi and (jxsi_in_gob or jxsi_supporting)) or (player_in_jxcat and (jxcat_in_gob or jxcat_supporting)))) and party_resources >= 1 and ((difficulty < 0 and strike_healthcare_relations >= 45) or (difficulty >= 0 and strike_healthcare_relations >= 55)) and government_budget >= 1 and healthcare_spending >= 0 and social_spending_cap >= 0 and not fla_escalated
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not ((player_party = "erc" and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting)) or (player_party = "cup" and (cup_in_gob or cup_supporting)) or (player_in_jxsi and (jxsi_in_gob or jxsi_supporting)) or (player_in_jxcat and (jxcat_in_gob or jxcat_supporting))): We are not part of the government nor providing external support to it. ?][? if party_resources < 1: Not enough resources. ?][? if ((difficulty < 0 and strike_healthcare_relations < 45) or (difficulty >= 0 and strike_healthcare_relations < 55)): Our relations with [+ strike_healthcare_partner +] are not good enough. ?][? if government_budget < 1: Not enough budget. ?][? if healthcare_spending < 0: Healthcare cuts need to be reversed before such a measure would even be possible. ?][? if social_spending_cap < 0: The current social spending cap is too low to allow for this. ?][? if fla_escalated: Stringent FLA conditions ban us from taking such action. ?]
on-arrival: strike_healthcare_response = "pressure"
go-to: resolve

@protest
title: Join the protests!
choose-if: not ((player_party = "erc" and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting)) or (player_party = "cup" and (cup_in_gob or cup_supporting)) or (player_in_jxsi and (jxsi_in_gob or jxsi_supporting)) or (player_in_jxcat and (jxcat_in_gob or jxcat_supporting)))
unavailable-subtitle: We're not welcome here, as we are currently supporting the government they are protesting against.
on-arrival: strike_healthcare_response = "protest"
go-to: resolve

@quiet
title: [? if (player_party = "erc" and erc_in_gob) or (player_party = "cup" and cup_in_gob) or (player_in_jxsi and jxsi_in_gob) or (player_in_jxcat and jxcat_in_gob): Back our partner's handling of the strike?][? if not ((player_party = "erc" and erc_in_gob) or (player_party = "cup" and cup_in_gob) or (player_in_jxsi and jxsi_in_gob) or (player_in_jxcat and jxcat_in_gob)) and ((player_party = "erc" and erc_supporting) or (player_party = "cup" and cup_supporting) or (player_in_jxsi and jxsi_supporting) or (player_in_jxcat and jxcat_supporting)): Leave this to the Generalitat to deal with?][? if not ((player_party = "erc" and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting)) or (player_party = "cup" and (cup_in_gob or cup_supporting)) or (player_in_jxsi and (jxsi_in_gob or jxsi_supporting)) or (player_in_jxcat and (jxcat_in_gob or jxcat_supporting))): Stay on the sidelines?]
on-arrival: strike_healthcare_response = "quiet"
go-to: resolve

@resolve
on-arrival: {!
    var response = Q.strike_healthcare_response;
    var option = this.game.scenes['strike_healthcare.' + response];
    var delivery = response == "accept" || response == "pressure";
    if (Q.strike_triggered == "healthcare" && !Q.cat_caretaker_gov &&
        Q.healthcare_spending >= -2 && Q.healthcare_spending < 2 &&
        option && this._runPredicate(option.viewIf, true) && this._runPredicate(option.chooseIf, true)) {
        var controlled = [Q.player_party].concat(Q.player_in_jxsi ? ["jxsi"] : [], Q.player_in_jxcat ? ["jxcat"] : []);
        Q.strike_triggered = null;
        Q.strike_healthcare_settled = delivery;
        if (delivery) {
            Q.government_budget -= 1;
            if (response == "pressure") Q.party_resources -= 1;
            G.registerLaw(Q, {id:"primary_care_workload_agreement", title:"Twelve minutes per patient settlement",
                fiscal_ticks:12,
                targets:{welfare_index_growth:0.10, social_dissent_eq:-2, generalitat_surplus:-0.0125}});
            if ((Q.cat_coalition || []).concat(Q.cat_coalition_support || []).some(function (party) { return controlled.includes(party); }) &&
                (Q.burdens_start_countdown > 0 || Q.burdens_start_trigger || Q.burdens_goal > 0 && Q.burdens_time > 0))
                Q.burdens_done += 1;
            // A narrow departmental agreement: fiscal effects settle over twelve
            // ticks; this strike owns its single electoral delivery award.
        }

        var cabinet = Array.from(new Set(Q.cat_coalition || []));
        function ballot(party) {
            if (party == "ciu") party = Q.parlament_current_ciu;
            if (party == "fl" || party == "federal_left") party = Q.parlament_current_icv;
            for (var list of ["jxsi", "jxcat"])
                if (Q[party + "_in_" + list] && (Q.parties || []).includes(list) &&
                    (Q.parlament_constituencies || []).some(function (province) {
                        return (Q.parlament_demographics || []).some(function (demo) { return Q[list + "_parlament_" + province + "_" + demo + "_support"] > 0; });
                    })) return list;
            return party;
        }
        var player = ballot(Q.player_party);
        cabinet = Array.from(new Set(cabinet.map(ballot)));
        var minister = ballot(Q.strike_healthcare_partner);
        var left = Array.from(new Set(["erc", "cup", Q.parlament_current_icv].map(ballot)))
            .filter(function (party) { return (Q.parties || []).includes(party); });
        var oppositionLeft = left.filter(function (party) { return !cabinet.includes(party) && party != player; });

        // Explicit province/demographic cells: no uniform national polling bonus.
        var profile = [
            ["barcelona","retired",0.55],
            ["barcelona","ind",0.35],
            ["barcelona","unemployed",0.30],
            ["barcelona","middle",0.20],
            ["girona","retired",0.65],
            ["girona","rural",0.50],
            ["girona","middle",0.25],
            ["girona","unemployed",0.20],
            ["lleida","retired",0.65],
            ["lleida","rural",0.55],
            ["lleida","middle",0.25],
            ["lleida","unemployed",0.20],
            ["tarragona","retired",0.60],
            ["tarragona","ind",0.40],
            ["tarragona","unemployed",0.30],
            ["tarragona","rural",0.25]
        ];
        var credit = [];
        if (delivery) {
            var partners = cabinet.filter(function (party) { return party != player; });
            credit.push([player, response == "pressure" ? 0.4 : partners.length ? 0.8 : 1]);
            if (response == "pressure") credit.push([minister,0.6]);
            else for (var party of partners) credit.push([party,0.2 / partners.length]);
        }
        // All routes use the shared conserving helper (including successor/list
        // resolution, donor caps and independence saturation).
        function transfer(from, to, amount, cell) {
            from = ballot(from); to = ballot(to);
            if (!from || !to || from == to || !(Q.parties || []).concat(["abstain"]).includes(from) ||
                !(Q.parties || []).concat(["abstain"]).includes(to)) return;
            G.cardSupportTransfer(Q, {contest:"parlament", from:from, to:to, amount:amount,
                maxDonorFraction:0.5, constituencies:[cell[0]], demographics:[cell[1]]});
        }
        for (var cell of profile) {
            var amount = cell[2];
            if (delivery) {
                for (var recipient of credit) {
                    var donors = recipient[0] == ballot("cup") ? [["fl",0.45],["erc",0.30],["abstain",0.25]] :
                        recipient[0] == ballot("erc") ? [["psc",0.45],["fl",0.30],["abstain",0.25]] :
                        [["psc",0.35],["fl",0.25],["abstain",0.40]];
                    for (var donor of donors) transfer(donor[0],recipient[0],amount * recipient[1] * donor[1],cell);
                }
            } else {
                // A silent opposition player does not collect the government's
                // losses. Other opposition parties still gain from mobilization.
                var challengers = oppositionLeft.slice();
                if (response == "protest" && !challengers.includes(player)) challengers.push(player);
                for (var incumbent of cabinet) {
                    var responsibility = incumbent == minister ? 1 : 0.4;
                    if (incumbent == player && incumbent != minister) responsibility = 0.6;
                    var destinations = challengers.filter(function (party) { return party != incumbent; });
                    for (var destination of destinations)
                        transfer(incumbent,destination,amount * responsibility * 0.6 / destinations.length,cell);
                    transfer(incumbent,"abstain",amount * responsibility * 0.2,cell);
                }
                for (var destination of challengers) {
                    transfer("psc",destination,amount * 0.10 / challengers.length,cell);
                    transfer("abstain",destination,amount * 0.10 / challengers.length,cell);
                }
                if ((Q.cat_coalition_support || []).some(function (party) { return controlled.includes(party); }) && !cabinet.includes(player)) {
                    for (var destination of oppositionLeft)
                        transfer(player,destination,amount * 0.25 / oppositionLeft.length,cell);
                }
            }
        }

        // Relations concern the actual parties, rather than pooled vote carriers.
        for (var party of ["erc", "cup", Q.parlament_current_icv]) {
            if (!controlled.includes(ballot(party)) && Number.isFinite(Q[party + "_relations"]))
                Q[party + "_relations"] += response == "quiet" ? -2 : 2;
        }
        if (response == "pressure" || response == "protest" || response == "quiet" && !controlled.includes(Q.strike_healthcare_partner) &&
            (Q.cat_coalition || []).concat(Q.cat_coalition_support || []).some(function (party) { return controlled.includes(party); }))
            Q[Q.strike_healthcare_partner + "_relations"] = (Q.strike_healthcare_relations || 0) + (response == "quiet" ? 2 : response == "pressure" ? -3 : -4);
    }
!}
call: generalitat_setpolicy

[? if strike_healthcare_settled: [? if response == "pressure" : Thanks to our efforts, ?][? if health_minister_gender = "m": Conseller ?][? if health_minister_gender = "f": Consellera ?]of Health [+ health_minister +] as reached an agreement with union representatives to expand primary-care staffing, managing this way to hold off the strikes, at least for now. ?]
[? if not strike_healthcare_settled: With angry workers on the street and a Ministry deeply against any concession that would put further strain on Generalitat finances, it looks like the labour dispute is here to stay. ?]

- @post_event: Continue
